# Full Production-Grade Migration & Backend Implementation

I want you to fully analyze the existing software before making any major changes.

Your task is to understand the complete frontend, dashboard, user flows, product structure, business logic, pages, components, forms, navigation, and the overall core idea of the application. After understanding the current system, convert it into a complete production-ready full-stack application.

## 1. First Analyze the Existing Application

Before writing or changing code:

* Analyze the entire existing frontend.
* Understand the purpose and core business idea of the software.
* Identify all public website pages.
* Identify all dashboard/admin pages.
* Identify all forms and actions.
* Identify all product-related functionality.
* Identify all existing data structures.
* Identify components that are currently using static/mock/hardcoded data.
* Identify functionality that currently exists only visually but has no backend.
* Understand how the public website and admin dashboard are supposed to work together.

Do not blindly rewrite the project.

Preserve the existing design, branding, layout, animations, responsiveness, and user experience unless there is a technical reason to change something.

---

# 2. Convert React Application to Next.js

The existing application is currently built with React.

Migrate the complete application to **Next.js** and use Next.js for both:

* Frontend
* Backend/API

Use the modern **Next.js App Router architecture**.

Organize the application professionally with proper separation between:

* Public website
* Admin/dashboard
* API/backend
* Database models
* Services
* Utilities
* Authentication
* Validation
* Components
* Server-side logic
* Client-side logic

Avoid unnecessary client components. Use Server Components wherever appropriate.

The final application should no longer depend on a separate React frontend and separate backend application unless absolutely necessary.

---

